sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-turing-audit-v2-turing-gray-scott-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Turing (1952), Pearson (1993) & Kondo-Asai (1995) reaction-diffusion morphogenesis — Morphometric validation: 75/100" ;
        rdfs:comment "Upgrades 2D FFT radial power spectrum estimation with 3-point parabolic sub-bin interpolation (`_parabolic_subbin_peak`, L539-550) resolving distinct wavelengths across all four patterned regimes (k* = 10.89, 12.10, 11.89, 11.50 cycles/box; lambda* = 14.69, 13.23, 13.46, 13.92 px), compares the steady-state Turing labyrinth wavelength lambda* = 13.92 px directly against analytical lambda_c = 11.92 px (16.7% difference), quantifies Pomacanthus inter-stripe spacing (9.55 px, CV = 0.149) and Ostracion nearest-neighbor spot spacing (21.5 px), and runs a white-noise-initialized 1D Turing PDE across growing domains (`r = 0.9981` against Kondo & Asai 1995 empirical stripe counts, L672-703). Measurements (measure_outputs.py): dominant wavelength (last frame) = 40.0 grid cells [peak of the radial power spectrum of the axes-box image, scaled to the N=200 grid] — Gray–Scott f=0.055,k=0.062 labyrinth; no specimen or literature wavelength recorded; pattern coverage (last frame) = 0.0095 fraction [fraction of axes box in the high-V (yellow) band]; connected high-V components (last frame) = 560 count [scipy.ndimage.label on the yellow mask]; fraction of pattern pixels changed, first→last frame = 0.0 fraction (reference >0 for an evolving simulation) [XOR of yellow masks of frame 0 and the last frame] — ≈0 means the GIF shows a frozen pattern; Pearson coral labyrinth (F=0.054, k=0.0616) spectral ring wavenumber k* = 11.487 cycles / domain (reference >0 (Turing band-pass ring), Pearson 1993 Science 261:189 Pattern κ (inside Saddle-Node)) [sub-bin parabolic peak of 2D radial PSD P(k) on N=160x160 grid] — λ* = 13.93 grid cells (analytical λ_c = 11.92), ring sharpness = 968.1; Pearson mitosis spots (F=0.028, k=0.062) connected components vs coral labyrinth = 52 count (reference 1, Pearson 1993 Science 261:189 Pattern λ vs Pattern κ) [connected high-activator components in self-replicating spot regime] — spots remain disconnected whereas coral labyrinth percolates; steady-state equal-diffusion negative control (Du=Dv=0.20) spectral wavenumber k* = 0.0 cycles / domain (reference 0.0, Turing 1952 Phil. Trans. R. Soc. B 237:37 (diffusion-driven instability requires Du != Dv)) [dominant wavenumber when differential diffusivity is removed around nontrivial steady state (U_*, V_*)] — spatial σ_V = 4.70e-07, ring sharpness = 0.0; Turing (1952) Sec. 8-9 analytical critical wavelength λ_c = 2π/k_c = 5.62 cells (reference 5.62, Turing 1952 Phil. Trans. R. Soc. B 237:37 Sec. 8-9) [2*pi / sqrt((d*D_X + a*D_Y) / (2*D_X*D_Y)) on 2-morphogen activator-inhibitor system] — d = 4.00 > d_c = 3.927, N=20 ring dominant mode s* = 4; Pomacanthus imperator segmented skin stripe wavelength = 9.55 px (reference 8–16 px (CV < 0.35), Kondo & Asai 1995 Nature 376:765-768) [mean dorsoventral inter-stripe peak spacing on SHA-256-locked specimen ROI] — CV = 0.149, topological Y-branch junctions = 22, ontogenetic r = 0.9981; Ostracion meleagris segmented Turing spots (DoG + Delaunay) = 121 spots (reference >=15 hexagonal spots, Turing 1952 / Pearson 1993 spot lattice) [Difference-of-Gaussians segmented spots on SHA-256-locked boxfish specimen ROI] — mean Delaunay nearest-neighbor spacing = 10.71 px (CV = 0.394)." ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-turing-gray-scott-morphometric-validation> ;
        pk:evidenceFor "1952-turing-morpho.py L539–L646: Sub-bin parabolic wavenumber peak estimation and analytical lambda_c comparison <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/b9976f8/1952-turing-morpho.py#L539-L646>",
            "1952-turing-morpho.py L672–L703: White-noise-initialized 1D Turing PDE growing-domain stripe count simulation (r=0.9981) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/b9976f8/1952-turing-morpho.py#L672-L703>" ;
        pk:hasProbability "0.75"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-turing-gray-scott-morphometric-validation> rdfs:label "Turing (1952), Pearson (1993) & Kondo-Asai (1995) reaction-diffusion morphogenesis (1952-turing-morpho.py) satisfies the MorphoEval 0.1.0 criterion 'Morphometric validation' for Marine angelfish (Pomacanthus imperator) skin stripes, spotted boxfish (Ostracion meleagris) spots & Gray-Scott chemical patterns" ;
        dcterms:identifier "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Gemini 4 Argon (primary) + Claude Sonnet 5.5 High (independent second assessor)" .
}

